        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "600fbf3f-b085-5809-b47a-d86aab7d81f7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Archduke John of Austria, Eugène de Beauharnais\n- Events: Battle of Sacile, Battle of Fontana Fredda, Clash at Pordenone, Revolutions of 1848\n- Organizations: House of Habsburg-Lorraine, German Empire\n- Roles: Austrian field marshal, Imperial regent\n\nFacts:\n- Archduke John of Austria was born on 20 January 1782 and was a member of the House of Habsburg-Lorraine.\n- On 15 April 1809, the Clash at Pordenone took place as a companion action to the Battle of Sacile.\n- On 16 April 1809, the Battle of Sacile, also known as the Battle of Fontana Fredda, ended with Archduke John of Austria's Austrian army defeating Eugène de Beauharnais's Franco-Italian army and forcing it to retreat.\n- During the Revolutions of 1848, Archduke John of Austria served as Imperial regent of the short-lived German Empire.\n- Archduke John of Austria was an Austrian field marshal and died on 11 May 1859.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
