        "text": "Page: Battle of Sacile. Sentence: The Battle of Sacile (also known as the Battle of Fontana Fredda) on 16 April 1809 and its companion Clash at Pordenone on 15 April saw an Austrian army commanded by Archduke John of Austria defeat a Franco-Italian army led by Eugène de Beauharnais and force it to retreat.\nPage: Archduke John of Austria. Sentence: Archduke John of Austria (German: \"Erzherzog Johann Baptist Joseph Fabian Sebastian von Österreich\" ; 20 January 1782 – 11 May 1859), a member of the House of Habsburg-Lorraine, was an Austrian field marshal and Imperial regent (\"Reichsverweser\") of the short-lived German Empire during the Revolutions of 1848.",
